+// Coalesced buffers are keyed on (and MPI tagged with) a partition id. Raw
+// MeshData partition ids restart at zero on every grid (the leaf grid and each
+// GMG level), so for multigrid grids we synthesize an id that is unique across
+// grids. Otherwise different GMG levels sharing a partition id would be merged
+// into (and tagged identically on) the same coalesced buffer. The mapping only
+// needs to be injective and stable on the sending rank, since receiving ranks
+// learn the ids from the buffer-info message.
+int CoalescedPartitionId(MeshData<Real> *pmd);
+
